-- Row il-77. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound readings kept beside the defects. They pass.
-- Each control shows that the test finds what it looks for where it is there, so that a failing test in pr77-tests-red.l4 is a finding and not a test that cannot succeed.
-- The expected values are written from the quotation lines in pr77-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the values there.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- I1 control 1: the 1965 page prints exactly the labels (9), (10), (11), (12), (13) from (9) to (13): the range was whole when written.
#ASSERT `the labels from a to b` `label (9)` `label (13)` (`the labels the 1965 page prints from (9) to (13)`'s `its labels`) EQUALS LIST `label (9)`, `label (10)`, `label (11)`, `label (12)`, `label (13)`
#ASSERT `every label from a to b is a label the printed list has there` `the labels the 1965 page prints from (9) to (13)` `label (9)` `label (13)` (`the labels the 1965 page prints from (9) to (13)`'s `its labels`)

-- I1 control 2: the instruction that inserts (11א) names (11) as the paragraph it follows, and the order test finds (11) before (11א) before (12).
#ASSERT `SH 2029 section 8 inserts paragraph (11 alef)`'s `it comes after the label` EQUALS JUST `label (11)`
#ASSERT `SH 2029 section 8 inserts paragraph (11 alef)`'s `the label it inserts` EQUALS JUST `label (11 alef)`
#ASSERT `the first label comes before the second in the list` `label (11)` `label (11 alef)` `the labels after the instructions whose commencement is established`
#ASSERT `the first label comes before the second in the list` `label (11 alef)` `label (12)` `the labels after the instructions whose commencement is established`

-- I1 control 3: the same for (11ב), which follows (11א).
#ASSERT `SH 2333 section 2 inserts paragraph (11 bet)`'s `it comes after the label` EQUALS JUST `label (11 alef)`
#ASSERT `the first label comes before the second in the list` `label (11 alef)` `label (11 bet)` `the labels after the instructions whose commencement is established`
#ASSERT `the first label comes before the second in the list` `label (11 bet)` `label (12)` `the labels after the instructions whose commencement is established`
#ASSERT NOT (`the first label comes before the second in the list` `label (12)` `label (11 alef)` `the labels after the instructions whose commencement is established`)

-- I1 control 4: the issue that wrote section 3 (the 1965 issue) and the issue that inserted (11א) (SH 2029) are two different issues, the second later.
#ASSERT `the two instruments are two different issues` `the 1965 issue` `SH 2029`
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 2029` `the 1965 issue`

-- I1 control 5: the words of section 3 contain the string "(9) עד (13)": the test finds the range when it is there.
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `section 3 as printed in 1965` "(9) עד (13)"
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` (`the range pointer in section 3`'s `the printed text that holds it`) (`the range pointer in section 3`'s `the pointer's words`)
#ASSERT `the range pointer in section 3`'s `the first label` EQUALS `label (9)`
#ASSERT `the range pointer in section 3`'s `the last label` EQUALS `label (13)`

-- I1 control 6: the insertion function puts the label where the instruction says, and leaves the list as it was for an instruction that inserts nothing.
#ASSERT elem `label (11 alef)` (`the labels after one insertion` `SH 2029 section 8 inserts paragraph (11 alef)` (`the labels the 1965 page prints from (9) to (13)`'s `its labels`))
#ASSERT `the labels after one insertion` `SH 2042 section 1 marks and adds after in section 6` (`the labels the 1965 page prints from (9) to (13)`'s `its labels`) EQUALS `the labels the 1965 page prints from (9) to (13)`'s `its labels`

-- I1 control 7: the test of the instructions whose commencement is established keeps an instruction whose commencement is printed and leaves out the one whose commencement is not established from a page.
#ASSERT elem `SH 2029 section 8 inserts paragraph (11 alef)` (`the instructions whose commencement is established` `the instructions on section 2(alef) in the order of their issue dates`)
#ASSERT NOT (elem `SH 2980 section 10(2) inserts paragraph (11 gimel)` (`the instructions whose commencement is established` `the instructions on section 2(alef) in the order of their issue dates`))

-- I2 control 1: subsection (ד) of section 3 is in the text of SH 1766 and no instruction is in the way: the test finds the subsection when it is there.
#ASSERT `the place is in the text as the instructions in the list left it` `subsection 3(dalet) of the Genetic Information Law` `subsection 3(dalet) as printed in SH 1766` EMPTY
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `subsection 3(dalet) as printed in SH 1766` "בדיקה גנטית להורות"

-- I2 control 2: an instruction of another kind at another place does not move the answer.
#ASSERT `the place is in the text as the instructions in the list left it` `subsection 3(dalet) of the Genetic Information Law` `subsection 3(dalet) as printed in SH 1766` (LIST `SH 2173 section 1(1) prints a definition in place of the one named`)

-- I2 control 3: the citing words of SH 2042 contain the string "סעיף 3(ד)", and both pointers.
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `paragraph (2) of subsection 6(gimel) as printed in SH 2042` "סעיף 3(ד)"
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` (`the pointers in paragraph 6(gimel)(2)`'s `the printed text that holds it`) (`the pointers in paragraph 6(gimel)(2)`'s `the pointer to a subsection, in its words`)
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` (`the pointers in paragraph 6(gimel)(2)`'s `the printed text that holds it`) (`the pointers in paragraph 6(gimel)(2)`'s `the pointer to a defined term, in its words`)

-- I2 control 4: the instrument that wrote the citing words (SH 2042, issue date 26.12.2005) is later than SH 1766 (25.12.2000) and earlier than SH 2173 (30.7.2008): the pointer was written while the subsection stood in the 2000 text.
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 2042` `SH 1766`
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 2173` `SH 2042`
#ASSERT NOT (`the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 1766` `SH 2042`)

-- I2 control 5: the defined term is in SH 1766, and SH 2173 section 1(1) names it as the definition it replaces.
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `the definition of the term as printed in SH 1766` "בדיקה גנטית להורות"
#ASSERT `the instruction names the words` `SH 2173 section 1(1) prints a definition in place of the one named` "בדיקה גנטית להורות"
